[{"text": "Observe a robot doing a two-stage pick-and-place task. Report visual facts ONLY.\nTask: pick up the alphabet soup and place it in the basket\nTarget appearance from the initial reference (identity only): The target is the small upright cylindrical can labeled 0, near the center behind the larger tomato sauce can and left of the basket. It has a dark gray metal top, a predominantly blue wrapper, and yellow-orange soup imagery around the lower portion. It is shorter and narrower than the foreground tomato sauce can, whose wrapper is mainly red and green. The target is distinct from the dark green dressing bottle and rectangular milk carton to its left.\nInitial reference keypoint labels: 0: alphabet_soup_1_main\n1: basket_1_main\n2: basket_1_main\n3: basket_1_main\n4: basket_1_main\n5: salad_dressing_1_main\n6: salad_dressing_1_main\n7: cream_cheese_1_main\n8: milk_1_main\n9: milk_1_main\n10: tomato_sauce_1_main\n11: butter_1_main\n\nIdentify the exact instructed object and the destination (basket in these tasks).\nThe initial image helps identify objects; only the CURRENT image describes the\ncurrent state. Do not infer success from a gripper command, a reward, a stage\ndescription, proximity, or what the robot was supposed to do.\n\nDistinguish an object next to the basket from one inside its interior. Overlap in\nthe image alone does not establish containment or support. If the basket rim,\nrobot or another object hides the target, use occluded/unknown. A closed gripper\nnear an object is not proof that the object is held. A target visibly suspended\nand supported by the fingers can be held. If grasp/contact is ambiguous, unknown.\nUse supported only when the target visibly rests on a surface; unsupported for\na suspended target; otherwise unknown. An open gripper does not prove placement.\nDescribe visible target location relative to the destination and fingers, and\nstate uncertainty. Never fabricate facts hidden behind the robot or basket wall.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object, no Markdown fences, no control decisions, with\nthese five keys and ONLY the following enum values:\ntarget_visibility: \"clear\", \"occluded\", or \"unknown\"\ntarget_location: \"outside_goal\", \"inside_goal\", \"above_goal\", or \"unknown\"\ngrasp: \"held\", \"not_held\", or \"unknown\"\nsupport: \"supported\", \"unsupported\", or \"unknown\"\nevidence: a short string giving visible supporting evidence and any uncertainty\n\nThe magenta circle marked TARGET locates the instructed target using its tracked keypoint in this CURRENT image. It is an identity aid only: it does not prove grasp, visibility, support, containment, or success. Judge visible evidence around that location; use unknown/occluded if hidden. Do not judge a different object left at the target's initial location. A point outside this image is not drawn; absence of a marker is not evidence of task completion.", "type": "text"}, {"text": "Current observation; judge this image", "type": "text"}, {"file": "image_01.png", "sha256": "86e79160b2c7b70da958e9502e60f26ac708c56ca37a08a51afdfa2caff0a030", "type": "image_url"}]